      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's exhausting to keep trying to force a narrative when the original plot has dissolved. You're not stuck on a page; you're in the necessary, messy aftermath where the ending doesn't make sense yet. Instead of waiting for a story to restart, consider that the ending itself is a complete, albeit painful, chapter. There is a profound, quiet dignity in simply letting the story rest, allowing yourself to be the quiet, unwritten space between the applause.",
